{
  "_comment": [
    "Site configuration. Edit and restart. Like config/logging.json this file is",
    "the whole story — no environment variables, except PORT, which still wins if",
    "it is set (handy for a one-off run without editing the file).",
    "",
    "  brand        the product name. Substituted for {{BRAND}} everywhere it is",
    "               written in public/*.html — the page title, the welcome panel,",
    "               the about panel, the share panel's second link. Change this",
    "               one value to rebrand the whole front end; no rebuild.",
    "  tagline      the one-line description under the name in both panels.",
    "               Substituted for {{TAGLINE}}.",
    "  titleSuffix  what follows the brand in the browser tab: the tab reads",
    "               'brand — titleSuffix'. Empty string = brand alone.",
    "  favicon      path (served from public/) to the tab icon. Point it at your",
    "               own .svg/.png/.ico and drop the file in public/.",
    "  port         HTTP + WebSocket listening port. The PORT environment",
    "               variable overrides it when set.",
    "",
    "  idleDisconnectMinutes",
    "               drop a call after this many minutes with no payload in",
    "               either direction — no keystroke from the user and nothing",
    "               from the BBS. Measured on payload, not on the carrier: the",
    "               modem sends audio continuously whether or not anyone is",
    "               typing, so an audio-based timer would never fire. Armed at",
    "               link-up, so a slow handshake is never counted as silence.",
    "               0 disables. Range 0..1440.",
    "  scrollbackLines",
    "               terminal scrollback ring, in lines. Served to the browser",
    "               as {{SCROLLBACK}} and read before the first byte is echoed",
    "               into it. Costs memory per open tab, not per server.",
    "               0 disables scrollback entirely. Range 0..100000.",
    "",
    "  directRequireListed",
    "               telnet bypass (the 'Telnet' speed entry) may only dial",
    "               boards the directory offers — either tier, after the",
    "               blacklist. A modem call is paced by its own handshake;",
    "               bypass connects the instant the dial arrives, so without",
    "               this the server is an open telnet proxy. true/false.",
    "  directMinIntervalSeconds",
    "               one telnet-bypass dial SERVER-WIDE per this many seconds —",
    "               shared by everyone, deliberately not per client: an abuser",
    "               has more addresses than a real visitor has patience, so a",
    "               per-IP bucket is what a rotating source defeats. Enforced as",
    "               a DELAY and never announced: dialling again too soon simply",
    "               takes longer to answer, and hanging up early buys back none",
    "               of it. Modem calls are not paced this way — the handshake",
    "               already does it — so under attack the worst case is that",
    "               bypass queues while every modem speed keeps working.",
    "               0 disables. Range 0..3600.",
    "",
    "  DIALLING LIMITS",
    "",
    "  connectTimeoutMs",
    "               give up on an outgoing BBS connect after this long, so a",
    "               black-holed board lands in telnetFailLog instead of hanging",
    "               until the OS gives up. MOVED HERE from config/logging.json:",
    "               how long to wait for a board is call behaviour, not a",
    "               logging preference. 0 disables. Range 0..120000.",
    "  resolveTimeoutMs",
    "               give up on a name lookup after this long. dns.lookup() has",
    "               no timeout of its own and inherits the resolver's, so with",
    "               `options timeout:2 attempts:3` and a search domain or two a",
    "               name that does not exist can take fifteen seconds to say so.",
    "               The caller hears silence for all of it, and getaddrinfo runs",
    "               on the libuv threadpool — four threads, shared with every",
    "               file write — so it is also the cheapest way to stall the",
    "               server. Keep it below the browser's dial tone (six seconds),",
    "               or the tone runs out before the answer arrives and the caller",
    "               gets silence again. 0 disables. Range 0..60000.",
    "  blockedPorts",
    "               ports this server will not dial on a host the directory does",
    "               NOT offer. THIS IS THE WHOLE PORT POLICY — lib/netguard.js",
    "               keeps no list and no default, so what is written here is",
    "               exactly what is refused and nothing else is. An empty list",
    "               blocks nothing; removing the setting blocks nothing. That is",
    "               a site decision to make, and its consequence to own.",
    "",
    "               Entries are a port (1433) or a range as a string (\"1-22\").",
    "               The shipped list refuses the whole well-known range EXCEPT",
    "               23, which is what a BBS answers on — that is why it reads",
    "               \"1-22\", \"24-1023\" rather than \"1-1023\", and it is also how",
    "               you would block telnet itself if you ever wanted to. The",
    "               ports above 1024 are the services worth reaching on somebody",
    "               else's machine; their INTERNAL equivalents are already",
    "               unreachable because of the address policy below.",
    "",
    "               A LISTED board is exempt from all of it. Some boards answer",
    "               on 80 or 443 to get through a restrictive firewall, and",
    "               refusing those would break real boards to close a hole a",
    "               listed destination does not open.",
    "",
    "               A MALFORMED ENTRY STOPS THE SERVER STARTING. Everything else",
    "               in this file falls back to a default and warns; a denial rule",
    "               must not, because one that quietly failed to parse reads as",
    "               protection and is not.",
    "",
    "               NOT configurable, and deliberately: the rule that a",
    "               destination must resolve to a PUBLIC address. Loopback,",
    "               RFC1918, link-local (169.254.169.254 is the cloud metadata",
    "               service), CGNAT and the rest are refused unconditionally in",
    "               lib/netguard.js, with no key here to turn it off. The only",
    "               way past it is the --allow-private-ips command-line flag,",
    "               which has to be typed on purpose and warns on every dial it",
    "               permits.",
    "  requireListedForAllDials",
    "               every dial must name a board the directory offers, not just",
    "               telnet bypass. OFF by default: turning it on removes manual",
    "               host:port entry, ATDT to an arbitrary address, and share or",
    "               embed links to unlisted boards, which are real features.",
    "               This is the lever to pull if the server is being abused.",
    "  maxSessions  at most this many WebSocket sessions at once, server-wide.",
    "               Each dialled session owns a software modem and a 5 ms",
    "               transmit timer, so this is the ceiling on what a flood can",
    "               cost. 0 disables. Range 0..10000.",
    "  maxPerBoardConcurrent",
    "               at most this many simultaneous connections to any ONE board,",
    "               server-wide, keyed on the RESOLVED address and port so two",
    "               names for the same machine cannot double the allowance.",
    "               This is the limit that protects the BOARDS rather than this",
    "               server: dial rate is already paced by the modem handshake,",
    "               and by directMinIntervalSeconds for telnet bypass. Over the",
    "               limit answers with the same reorder tone every other failed",
    "               connect gets. 0 disables. Range 0..1000.",
    "  noDialTimeoutSeconds",
    "  carrierTimeoutSeconds",
    "               close a socket that never dials, and a dial that never",
    "               reaches carrier. Both are abandoned calls holding a modem",
    "               the idle timer cannot see (it is armed at link-up, so a slow",
    "               handshake is never mistaken for silence). Neither costs a",
    "               visitor anything: the page opens a fresh WebSocket for every",
    "               Connect, so these can only close a call nobody is on.",
    "               0 disables either. Range 0..3600.",
    "",
    "  splashFadeSeconds",
    "               how long the pre-roll splash (public/splash/) takes to fade",
    "               out once the page is up, in seconds. The splash plays from",
    "               the first paint on the lowest layer, the app assembles over",
    "               it, and the fade starts when the terminal has drawn, the",
    "               fonts have settled and the welcome panel — if it showed — has",
    "               been closed. Nothing waits for it and nothing it can do",
    "               fails the page. 0 removes it the moment the app is ready,",
    "               with no fade. Range 0..30.",
    "",
    "  SYSOP STATUS PAGE",
    "",
    "  sysopEnabled A read-only status page at /sysop, polling /sysop.json:",
    "               calls in progress and what they are dialled to, session",
    "               lengths, today's and all-time dial counts, and the limits",
    "               this server is running under. Read-only — there is no",
    "               control on the page and no route behind it that writes.",
    "               OFF by default. With this false, or either setting below",
    "               empty, both paths answer 404 rather than 401: an operator",
    "               who has not turned it on looks exactly like a build that",
    "               does not have it, which is all a scanner ever learns.",
    "  sysopUser    the username for the HTTP Basic prompt.",
    "  sysopPasswordHash",
    "               the password, hashed. Generate it with",
    "",
    "                   node tools/sysoppass.js",
    "",
    "               which prompts with the echo off and prints the line to",
    "               paste. NOT the password itself: this file lives on disk, in",
    "               backups, and possibly in a repository. The hash carries its",
    "               own scrypt parameters, so raising the cost in a later",
    "               version will not invalidate a line minted today. A value",
    "               that is not a hash this server can read STOPS STARTUP —",
    "               pasting the password in by mistake is caught at boot rather",
    "               than at the prompt.",
    "",
    "               Basic sends the credential on every request, so it is worth",
    "               exactly as much as the transport. Behind TLS (or a tunnel,",
    "               or Cloudflare) that is fine; on a bare-http origin the",
    "               password crosses the LAN in the clear on every poll.",
    "  sysopRefreshSeconds",
    "               how often the page re-polls. Each poll is one authenticated",
    "               request answered from counters already in memory, and the",
    "               credential check is memoised for five minutes so the",
    "               password hash does not re-run on a timer. Range 1..3600."
  ],

  "brand": "SynthLink",
  "tagline": "A BBS terminal that dials over a real software modem.",
  "titleSuffix": "modem-carried web BBS terminal",
  "favicon": "/favicon.svg",
  "port": 8088,
  "idleDisconnectMinutes": 30,
  "scrollbackLines": 5000,
  "directRequireListed": true,
  "directMinIntervalSeconds": 10,

  "connectTimeoutMs": 5000,
  "resolveTimeoutMs": 5000,
  "blockedPorts": [
    "1-22", "24-1023",
    1433, 1521, 2049, 2375, 2376, 2379, 3306, 3389, 5432,
    5900, 5901, 5984, 6379, 6443, 9200, 9300, 11211, 27017
  ],
  "requireListedForAllDials": false,
  "maxSessions": 50,
  "maxPerBoardConcurrent": 10,
  "noDialTimeoutSeconds": 60,
  "carrierTimeoutSeconds": 120,

  "splashFadeSeconds": 4,

  "sysopEnabled": false,
  "sysopUser": "",
  "sysopPasswordHash": "",
  "sysopRefreshSeconds": 5
}
